// the thing this project is actually about, had no front door -- which is the standing rule applied one level up
// from where it usually bites.
//
// EVERY ENTRY MUST NAME ITS EXACT KEY. That is the point of the collection: not "here are some simulations" but
// "here is what each one is graded against, and by what". An instrument without a key is decoration, and an
// index that let one in would be advertising decoration.
//
// The gate reads this file and checks it against the filesystem and the device registry, so an entry cannot
// describe a page that does not exist, name a gate that was deleted, or quietly omit a new instrument.
