        key: "The idea is ACE's (arXiv 2510.04618); none of the code is, and the dependency is refused. THE ROUNDHOUSE ALREADY HAD TWO OF THE THREE ROLES AND ITS REFLECTOR IS BETTER THAN THE PAPER'S: deviceCritic is DETERMINISTIC, so it cannot hallucinate, rate-limit or be charged for, and it names the defect from a fixed list -- ACE's Reflector infers what worked from traces with no ground truth. What was missing was persistence. *** THE SCOPE IS NARROWER THAN ACE'S ON PURPOSE: only the five MALFORMED reasons trigger a strategy. *** modelBench separates MALFORMED (an interface failure a hint can fix) from REFUSED (well-formed and wrong, where 'only a better model fixes this'), so a book that mined REFUSED would be teaching a model to guess luckier. Constructing a strategy on an invented trigger THROWS. *** AND A STRATEGY IS NEVER INJECTED UNTIL A TWO-ARM TRIAL MEASURES IT. *** The control arm is what ACE has not got: a Reflector mining 'what worked' sees only the runs that happened, so a model that improved on its own gets credited to whatever strategy was added that week. Measured: a hint dropping the rate 0.650 -> 0.050 over 40 questions is PROVEN; an identical-arm hint (0.650 -> 0.650) is RETIRED and KEPT WITH ITS NUMBERS, because 'we tried this and it did nothing' is a result nobody should rediscover; 0.900 -> 0.100 on n=4 is still PROPOSED, because four runs is a rumour. State is DERIVED on load, so hand-editing 'proven' into the JSON buys nothing -- the licence ratchet from proposers.mjs applied to strategies. THE SHIPPED BOOK IS EMPTY: ACE ships strategies mined from someone else's traces, and a strategy untried on THIS tree's devices has no evidence here.",
