        key: "*** THE PROPERTY IS <P x, y> = <x, P^T y> AND NEITHER FILE EVER STATES IT. *** Measured on a real hierarchy -- solid shell, a solid obstacle and an AIR lid, so the coarse type field carries structure and the type filters in both transfers actually fire -- the worst relative gap is 2.2e-16 at 16x16, 7.2e-16 at 32x32 and 1.1e-15 at 64x64, across every level pair. THE INNER PRODUCT IS ASSERTED NON-TRIVIAL BESIDE IT, because two zeros are adjoint too. *** WHAT MAKES IT A KEY RATHER THAN A RESTATEMENT IS THAT IT IS NOT STRUCTURAL HERE. In multigrid.mjs one weight helper (_pcols) serves both directions, so the scatter pair is adjoint BY CONSTRUCTION and could not fail -- measured as a CONTROL at the same precision, 6.3e-16. The port rewrote both directions as GATHERS, and in that form the identity survives only if the restriction's window covers every fine cell whose interpolation stencil reaches the coarse cell. Nothing says so. *** THE WINDOW IS BRACKETED FROM BOTH SIDES, which is what makes it a measurement rather than a preference: the shipped window is [2c-1 .. 2c+2]; NARROWER (the 2x2 block -- the obvious 'one coarse cell owns four fine cells' rewrite) breaks the identity by 1.4e-1 at 32x32; WIDER reproduces the shipped inner product TO THE LAST BIT, so the extra cells contribute exactly zero. The shipped window is the NARROWEST one that works. AND THE HONEST LIMIT ON ITS NOVELTY: truncating the window ALSO reddens multigridGPU-selfcheck's existing parity check (9.2e-2 at 32x32), so this key is not the only thing that would catch that defect and claiming otherwise would inflate it. What it adds is that it is REFERENCE-FREE -- parity is only ever as right as PoissonMG and is blind by construction to a defect the two share -- and EXACT, so the bar is machine epsilon rather than a percentage somebody can decide to live with. *** NOT GRADED, AND IT IS THE BIGGEST LIMIT: THE WGSL. There is no WebGPU in the sandbox, GpuMultigrid never runs, and this grades the JS SHADOW whose indexing is identical to the shaders BY CLAIM. wgslGraded is reported as 0 as DATA rather than as a sentence, because a limit that lives only in prose is one nothing can read.",
